## Find the bus arriving between 18:00 and 21:00 (part i)
Read the Waterford Bus Station row: A 12:00, B 14:00, C 16:15, D 20:30, E 22:15, F 01:10.
Only $20{:}30$ (bus D) is between $18{:}00$ and $21{:}00$.
## Find the journey time of bus B (part ii)
Bus B leaves Dublin Airport at 10:50 and arrives at 14:00.
10{:}50 \text{ to } 11{:}00 &= 10 \text{ minutes}
11{:}00 \text{ to } 14{:}00 &= 3 \text{ hours}
10 \text{ min} + 3 \text{ h} &= 3 \text{ h } 10 \text{ min}
ANSWER: \text{Bus D}, \quad 3 \text{ h } 10 \text{ min}

## Factorise the right-hand side (part ii)
P &= rh + 2rt
P &= r(h + 2t)
## Divide both sides by h + 2t
\frac{P}{h + 2t} &= r
r &= \frac{P}{h + 2t}
## Substitute P = 892.5, h = 35, t = 8 (part iii)
r &= \frac{892.5}{35 + 2(8)}
&= \frac{892.5}{35 + 16}
&= \frac{892.5}{51}
&= 17.5
The new hourly rate is €17.50.
ANSWER: r = \frac{P}{h + 2t}, \quad r = 17.5

## Change 7 minutes to seconds
7 \times 60 &= 420 \text{ seconds}
## Find the number of full sets
One set takes $80$ seconds. Try $5$ sets.
5 \times 80 &= 400 \text{ seconds}
420 - 400 &= 20 \text{ seconds left}
## Find the distance in the last 20 seconds
Run 1 takes 10 seconds (38 m), then the rest takes 10 seconds, using all 20 seconds. Dean runs $38$ m.
## Add the distances
5 \times 164 &= 820
820 + 38 &= 858 \text{ m}
ANSWER: 858 \text{ m}

## Change the distance to metres
5 \times 1000 &= 5000 \text{ m}
## Change the time to seconds
25 \times 60 &= 1500 \text{ s}
## Use speed = distance ÷ time
\text{Speed} &= \frac{5000}{1500}
&= 3.33\ldots
&\approx 3.3
ANSWER: 3.3 \text{ m/s}

## Read the height of the slide (part i)
Points B and C are both at $y = 2$, so the slide is $2$ m high.
## Find the length BC (part ii)
B has $x = -0.4$ and C has $x = 0$.
BC &= 0 - (-0.4)
&= 0.4 \text{ m}
## Change metres to centimetres
0.4 \times 100 &= 40 \text{ cm}
ANSWER: 2 \text{ m}, \quad 40 \text{ cm}

## Find the total work in employee-hours
13 \times 4 &= 52
## Find the work done in the first 2 hours
4 \times 2 &= 8
## Subtract to find the work left
52 - 8 &= 44
## Divide by the 3 remaining employees
\frac{44}{3} &= 14\tfrac{2}{3} \text{ hours}
## Change the fraction of an hour to minutes
\tfrac{2}{3} \times 60 &= 40 \text{ minutes}
## Write the time in hours and minutes
14\tfrac{2}{3}\text{ hours} &= 14 \text{ hours } 40 \text{ minutes}
ANSWER: 14 \text{ h } 40 \text{ min}

## (ii) Probability that School B plays in the final
Row B of the table has 4 pairings (BW, BX, BY, BZ) out of 16.
P(B) &= \frac{4}{16}
&= \frac{1}{4}
## (iii) Count the pairings now that D has withdrawn
Group 1 is now A, B, C, so the table has $3 \times 4 = 12$ equally likely pairings.
B but not Z: BW, BX, BY, which is 3 pairings.
Z but not B: AZ, CZ, which is 2 pairings.
## (iii) Add the pairings and divide by 12
P(\text{B or Z, not both}) &= \frac{3 + 2}{12}
&= \frac{5}{12}
ANSWER: \text{(ii) } \tfrac{1}{4} \qquad \text{(iii) } \tfrac{5}{12}
